  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Every row singles out the contradictory class, on the 8- and 10-line glues",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "On the 8-line and 10-line trisum glues (TRISUM-READ's seeds 3 and 6; seed 36's glue is isomorphic to seed 6's), exactly one switching class has no solution, the class of the generator's Pfaffian signing, whose plain edge-atom spaces are three-fold, and every single row of creation between glue lines singles it out: for every line a, no other class of the glue without a has the same row a. In the glue without a, line a's three points are tied for that class and for no other. In its row, every line sharing two points with a is degenerate, and at each line that shares two points with no other line the degenerate entries alone single the class out.",
  "dependencies": [
    "SWITCH-COMPLETE-20261108-001B",
    "SWITCH-PROOF-20261108-001A",
    "TRISUM-READ-20261107-001A"
  ],
